diff --git a/patches/phosh/0019-layer-surface-output-at-construction.patch b/patches/phosh/0019-layer-surface-output-at-construction.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..be6dcb7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/patches/phosh/0019-layer-surface-output-at-construction.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+From: luma-duo2
+Subject: layersurface: set wl-output at construction
+
+"wl-output" was an ordinary property, so GObject set it only after
+constructed() had run. PhoshLockscreen creates its background surface in
+constructed() from phosh_layer_surface_get_wl_output(), which therefore
+always returned NULL: the background was created with no output and the
+compositor placed it on an output of its own choosing. With one output that
+is the right one. With two (Surface Duo 2), phoc can place it on the other
+panel, and stacking it below the lock screen then fails with "Layer surface
+not on same output", a protocol error that ends the session.
+
+Make the property construct-only, as every caller already treats it, so it
+is set before constructed() runs.
+
+--- a/src/layersurface.c
++++ b/src/layersurface.c
+@@ -474,7 +474,7 @@
+       "wl-output",
+       "Wayland Output",
+       "The wl_output associated with this surface",
+-      G_PARAM_READWRITE | G_PARAM_STATIC_STRINGS);
++      G_PARAM_READWRITE | G_PARAM_CONSTRUCT_ONLY | G_PARAM_STATIC_STRINGS);
+ 
+   props[PHOSH_LAYER_SURFACE_PROP_ANCHOR] =
+     g_param_spec_uint (
